# Exclusions, beyond checks that just don't apply (e.g. llvm-*, fuchsia-*):
#   bugprone-throwing-static-initialization the self-registering TEST_CASE idiom is inherently
#   cert-err58-cpp                          static-init; the same finding under two check names
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays        the GSL span/at() bounds-safety profile isn't in use;
#   modernize-avoid-c-arrays                 CLI code deals in argv-shaped C arrays by nature
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers   ad hoc literals (test expectations, column widths)
#   readability-magic-numbers                are idiomatic here, not worth naming
#   cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage           the public API is macros (CHECK/REQUIRE/...)
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-*          the GSL span/at() bounds-safety profile isn't in use
#   modernize-use-trailing-return-type      not this codebase's return-type style
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once          `#pragma once` is this codebase's header-guard style
#   readability-avoid-const-params-in-decls conflicts with the east-const style used consistently
#                                            across both declarations and definitions
#   readability-braces-around-statements   conflicts with AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine
#   readability-identifier-length           short names (e, s, fn, ...) are used deliberately
#   readability-implicit-bool-conversion    flags idiomatic pointer truthiness (if (ptr))
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -readability-avoid-const-params-in-decls,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-magic-numbers

HeaderFilterRegex: '.*'
WarningsAsErrors: ''
